--  A replacement of a running process by a new version of its program
--  (ADR 0032, #866), which mem makes with Replacer.Replace_Process. Mem
--  serves one call at a time, and both versions page-fault to it during
--  the handover, so it can't launch the new version itself: the holder
--  of the replacement does, and mem does the privileged steps.
--
--  1. Ready is True once the old version is between calls, blocked
--     receiving. The caller asks until it is, up to a limit of its own.
--  2. The caller launches the new version against Bank, the bank that
--     the old version's own bank is a sub-bank of, so that the two banks
--     are siblings.
--  3. Allow, with the new version's command endpoint, lets the new
--     version's calls, and only those, reach the old version, whose
--     other calls are held.
--  4. The caller makes the new version's launch call, with the old
--     version's Replaceable as its Previous argument. The new version
--     takes over the old one's state, caps and deferred calls.
--  5. Commit, once that call has completed, makes the switch: the new
--     version takes the old one's identity and bank tree, the held calls
--     reach it, and mem ends the old version. It is False, and nothing
--     changed, if the switch couldn't be made: the new version lacks an
--     endpoint of the old one's, the old version is in a call, or a call
--     is queued for it. Mem is a boot module, whose operations can't
--     fail by raising, so Commit says whether it committed.
--
--  Releasing a replacement that didn't commit fails the handover: mem
--  ends the new version, if there is one, and releases the held calls to
--  the old version, which goes on as it was, and takes back the reply
--  caps of its deferred calls (#879). After a Commit, Release only ends
--  the replacement.

interface Replacement : Resource is

   function Ready return Boolean;

   function Bank return interface Bank;

   procedure Allow (New_Version : Capability);

   function Commit return Boolean;

end Replacement;
